# =============================================================================
# cassette_signaltap.qsf.snippet -- QSF additions for the X76F100 SECURITY
# CASSETTE read probe (root-causing the hypbbc2p installer -11N that survives a
# clean rebuild: sim PASSES Gate A, silicon FAILS it).
#
# HOW IT BECOMES ACTIVE: append this to Konami_System_573.qsf on the DEBUG
# branch (dbg-signaltap-cassette), committed together with
# tools/signaltap_573/cassette_read.stp -- the hub launcher builds a pushed git
# ref, so both files must be committed on the ref built. NEVER merge this into
# feat-flash-load / main: debug-build-only. The vendored psx/ is untouched
# (preservation is QSF-only).
#
# REQUIRED SECOND STEP (RUNBOOK 1b): the compiler does NOT read the .stp;
# insertion is driven by the SLD_* expansion generated ON DELL by
#   quartus_stp Konami_System_573 --stp_file tools/signaltap_573/cassette_read.stp --enable
# then commit the expanded QSF.
#
# NODE PRESERVATION (RUNBOOK gates):
#   * data[] is M10K block RAM (x76f100.v) -- its cells are UNTAPPABLE. We watch
#     the read PORT (data_rdata/rd_addr/rd_oob) and write PORT (ram_*) instead.
#   * ALL 70 taps are real registers -> PRESERVE_REGISTER (no KEEP). The bit-bang
#     lines are tapped at the REGISTERED seccart latch d_q[4:0] (SDA/SCL/CS/RST/
#     DS2401), NOT the folded x76f100 input pins: Quartus 17.0 REJECTS a
#     `set_instance_assignment -name KEEP ON` (Error 125048 -- KEEP is an RTL
#     synthesis attribute, not a QSF assignment name). sda_o (the device output
#     reg) == sec_io0 for an X76F100 so it doubles as the seccart readback.
#   * NO WILDCARDS (Quartus 17.0 silently ignores wildcard PRESERVE_* ->
#     Critical Warning 136017 -> swept tag regs -> trigger can never fire).
#     Every assignment is an explicit full per-bit path.
#
# Clock-domain note: the cassette/seccart are ENTIRELY clk_1x. The acq clock in
# the .stp is the clk_1x PLL net (outclk_wire[0]) -- so NO oversampling, NO
# aliasing (cleaner than the CLUT clk_2x probe). All taps below are clk_1x.
#
# REGENERATE this snippet (keep it in lockstep with the watch list):
#   tclsh tools/signaltap_573/cassette_qsf_gen.tcl > tools/signaltap_573/cassette_signaltap.qsf.snippet

# Generated by gen_qsf.tcl -- DO NOT hand-edit (regenerate to match the watch list).
set_global_assignment -name ENABLE_SIGNALTAP ON

# --- state (reg) ---
